---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "10 Apps You Need to Download Before Traveling to China";
const description = "The apps you need to survive and thrive in China — payment, transport, translation, and more.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/en/life/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Life
      </a>
    </nav>
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">📱 Life in China</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        10 Apps You Need to Download Before Traveling to China
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Forget Google and Facebook — here is what you actually need.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

        <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-green-800 leading-relaxed">
        China runs on apps. Forget Google and Facebook — here you need <strong>WeChat</strong> for messaging and paying, <strong>Alipay</strong> for shopping, <strong>Didi</strong> for rides, and <strong>Amap</strong> for directions. Download these <strong>before</strong> you arrive, because some (like Google services) are harder to access once you're inside China.
      </p>
    </div>

        <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#payment" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">💳 Payment Apps</a></li>
        <li><a href="#messaging" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">💬 Messaging & Social</a></li>
        <li><a href="#transport" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚗 Transport & Navigation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#travel" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏨 Travel Booking</a></li>
        <li><a href="#translation" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🔤 Translation & Language</a></li>
        <li><a href="#food" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🍜 Food & Discovery</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="payment" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">💳</span> Payment Apps
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">💬 WeChat (微信)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">China's super-app. You'll use it to message, pay at stores, split bills, order food, book appointments, and more. Almost every business in China accepts WeChat Pay — from fancy restaurants to street food stalls. Set it up with a credit card (Visa/Mastercard), and you're good to go.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">💳 Alipay (支付宝)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The other half of China's payment duopoly. Alipay is particularly strong for online shopping (Taobao, Tmall). Like WeChat, it can be used in various payment scenarios, as well as on practical mini-programs such as public transportation and shared bicycles.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="messaging" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">💬</span> Messaging & Social
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">💬 WeChat</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Yes, WeChat is also your messaging app. Everyone communicates via WeChat — tour guides will coordinate via WeChat groups, and local contacts will expect you to have it. Forget WhatsApp, no one uses it domestically.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="transport" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🚗</span> Transport & Navigation
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-purple-50 border border-purple-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-purple-900 mb-3">🚗 Didi (滴滴出行)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">China's ride-hailing app. You can enter your destination in English, see the fare upfront, and pay with Alipay or WeChat. Works in every major city. Use it instead of hailing taxis — you'll avoid communication issues, and it's cheaper.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-orange-50 border border-orange-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-orange-900 mb-3">🗺️ Amap (高德地图) or Baidu Maps (百度地图)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Google Maps doesn't provide turn-by-turn navigation in China. These two are the local alternatives. They work for driving, public transit, walking, and even finding nearby restaurants. Both have some English support, but Baidu Maps is slightly more foreigner-friendly.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-indigo-900 mb-3">🏨 Trip.com (携程)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The English version of Ctrip — China's largest travel booking platform. Book flights, trains, hotels, and attractions. Has full English support and accepts foreign credit cards.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="translation" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🔤</span> Translation & Language
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-3">🌐 Google Translate</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The most reliable option. Download the Chinese language pack for offline use. The camera translation feature is invaluable for menus, signs, and packaging.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-3">📖 Pleco</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The gold standard for Chinese-English dictionaries. It supports photo and voice translation, so it's really handy for all sorts of situations.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="food" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🍜</span> Food & Discovery
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">⭐ Dianping (大众点评)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">China's Yelp. Find restaurants by cuisine, price, location, and rating. The interface is Chinese-only, but the photos and maps are easy to navigate. Use it to discover hidden local gems.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">🍜 Amap Street Food Ranking (高德扫街榜)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A hidden gem inside Amap. This feature ranks restaurants based on real user behavior — how many people actually navigated there, how many went back multiple times, and how many traveled a long distance just to eat there. Unlike Dianping (where reviews can be bought), the 扫街榜 is based on <strong>real footsteps</strong>, and Amap has publicly stated it will <strong>never accept paid listings</strong>.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">Just open Amap → search "扫街榜" → and see what locals are actually eating near you. It's perfect for travelers who want to skip tourist traps and find the real deal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 Related Guides</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/en/life/survival-kit/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🎒 Your China Trip Survival Kit</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">The master checklist for your trip</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/life/sim-card-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">📶 Best SIM Card & eSIM for Tourists</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Stay connected with data plans</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💳 How to Set Up Alipay</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Connect your card in minutes</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/payment/setup-wechat/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💬 How to Set Up WeChat Pay</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">WeChat is essential for China</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  
    <!-- Sources -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Sources</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li>App recommendations based on practical travel experience.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>